# LF is mandatory for these, not a preference.
#
# The files below are executed by bash under WSL2 -- the deploy pipeline
# (scripts/*.sh), the git hooks that trigger it (.githooks/*), and the
# Dockerfile that docker parses. They are also copied straight out of the
# working tree and executed (scripts/infra-watchdog.sh runs every minute from
# cron as /home/cap/infra-watchdog.sh), so whatever is on disk is what runs.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set for the Windows git on this machine, with no
# attributes file overriding it. On the next checkout that touches one of these
# files, git would write CRLF and bash would then fail on every line with
# `$'\r': command not found` -- silently, from a deploy that looks like it ran.
# Pinning eol=lf makes git write LF regardless of autocrlf.
*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
